<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101741" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφρῐγ-άω</span></b>  [v. fin.], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be full to bursting, to be plump</i>, esp.
			of a woman's breasts, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.71
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔθατα ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.250
			</span></i>: then, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			generally, of young persons, high-fed horses, etc., <i>to be fresh,
				vigorous, in full health and strength</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέῳ τε καὶ σφριγῶντι σώματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					196
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐσωματεῖ καὶ σφριγᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					799
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφριγᾷ τὸ σῶμά σου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					80
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ σώματα σφριγῶντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					840b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥβῃ σφριγῶντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Achae.
					4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μύες</span> (muscles) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφριγῶντες, ὡς ἂν εἴποι τις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archig.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.91
			</span></i>; of animals, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφριγῶσα ἡμίονος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					1322.34
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόες τὸν αὐχένα σφριγῶντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					3.1
				</span></i>
			; of trees, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δένδρα σφριγῶντα νέοις
				κλωσίν</span>
			<i>luxuriant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βότρυες σφριγῶντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.Chr.
					7.75
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδίᾳ καὶ γαλήνῃ ς</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>full-blooded, swollen</i> with passion or pride, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφριγῶντα θυμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					382
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦθον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					478
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>swell with desire, be at heat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				3.368
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν σφριγώντων ἐν λόγοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					276
				</span></i>
			: c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				14.5
			</span></i>. Chiefly used in the pres.
			part. [In <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
			</span></i> l.c., for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφρῑγᾷ</span> Lobeck
			conjectured <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφρῐγάᾳ</span>.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
